live-draw: FP16 textures keep their format, F_X32 colour surfaces render to R32_FLOAT.

Symptom (Killzone 3 first level, RPCS3 capture of pass 11): Y16_X16_FLOAT (0x9F) textures, 172 binds per frame,
were not decoded at all (the unit read SRV_WHITE); W16Z16Y16X16_FLOAT textures were decoded to RGBA8, clamped to
[0,1] with negatives forced to 0, which loses the HDR range of the FP16 buffers the composite reads; the one
F_X32 colour surface was rendered into RGBA8, clamping and quantising the float it stores.

Fix:
- decode_guest_texture_float: both FP16 formats (2D and cube, swizzled or pitch-linear, mips as the RGBA8 path)
  upload as R16G16B16A16_FLOAT / R16G16_FLOAT; each big-endian half is byte-swapped, the first half in memory is
  component R (X), then G (Y), B (Z), A (W). The 3D path keeps the old RGBA8 decode.
- write_texture_srv: the RSX remap becomes the SRV Shader4ComponentMapping (ld_float_tex_mapping), so texels stay
  bit-exact. Source channel (A,R,G,B) -> component: W16Z16Y16X16 W,X,Y,Z; Y16_X16 Y,X,Y,X (ASSUMPTION: the RSX's
  two-channel fill; KZ3 uses remap 0x29E4 = (X, Y, 0, 1), which never selects B or A from the source).
- ld_color_dxgi: F_X32 (0xD) surfaces are R32_FLOAT; render state carries rt_x32 into the PSO RTV format and key.
- rsx_live_draw_debug_read_surface: raw texel readback of a host surface, for host tests.

Verified with tools/smoke/test_tex_float.c (host test under Proton): 4x4 FP16 textures with values up to 1920.0
and negatives, three remaps, FP16 and F_X32 surfaces, all texels compared bit-exactly.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

